{title: 476 - Burdens Are Lifted at Calvary}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #476 • ( HYMN SETTING) • 8.7.9.6}
{lyricist: John M. Moore}
{composer: John M. Moore}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 476}
{meta: tune ( HYMN SETTING)}
{meta: meter 8.7.9.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Days are filled with sor-row and [C7]care,
[C7]Hearts are lonely and [F]drear;
[Bb]Burdens are lifted [F]at Calvary,
[C7]Jesus is [F]very near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]Burdens are lifted [F]at Calvary,
[F]Calvary, Calvary,
[Bb]Burdens are lifted [F]at Calvary,
[C7]Jesus is [F]very near.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Cast your care on Jesus today,
[C7]Leave your worry and [F]fear;
[Bb]Burdens are lifted [F]at Calvary,
[C7]Jesus is [F]very near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Troubled soul, the Saviour [Bb/F]can [F]see,
[C7]Ev'ry heartache and [F]tear;
[Bb]Burdens are lifted [F]at Calvary
[C7]Jesus is [F]very near.
{end_of_verse}
